  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive stakeholder dialogue for effective implementation of financial security for mine rehabilitation and environmental compliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity supported the Ministry of Mines&#x2019; Directorate for Environmental Protection to organise two multi-stakeholder workshops in the Haut-Katanga and Lualaba regions. These sessions brought together over 200 participants from government, mining companies, banks, civil society, and international partners to raise awareness and strengthen compliance with the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)&#x2019;s legal obligation for financial guarantees for mine site rehabilitation. The goal was to improve environmental governance, promote transparency, and reduce the climate and biodiversity impacts of mining operations.</narrative>
  </description>
